import RequestProject.Wikidata.NamedGraphs
import RequestProject.Epistemic.Bridge

/-!
# Importing a property-path answer as evidence

`RequestProject.Epistemic.QueryEvidence` imports answers to the core query
fragment, where the discipline turns on which side of the monotonicity line the
query lives.  Property paths are all on the good side — `holds_mono` says so —
so the interesting question moves from the *shape of the query* to the *scope it
was asked of*:

* an answer to a path is stable under growth (`path_support_is_stable`), so
  importing it as support is sound;
* support obtained inside one named graph transfers to the whole dataset
  (`graph_support_transfers_up`);
* and it does **not** transfer the other way (`dataset_support_is_not_graph_support`):
  the derived answer of the two-source dataset leaves both of its named graphs
  unresolved.  Attribution of a derived answer to a source is therefore not
  available, which is `derived_fact_need_not_hold_in_any_graph` at the level of
  evidence.

Import stays fail-closed (`PathCertificate.state_ne_contradicted`): a path that
does not relate the reported items yields `unresolved`, never `contradicted`.
-/

